---
description: Prefer Tailwind inline classes over custom CSS in style.css
alwaysApply: true
---

# Tailwind inline first

Put styles on the element with Tailwind utility classes in PHP/HTML templates. Do **not** add rules to `assets/css/style.css` when the same result can be achieved inline.

## Do

```html
<div
  class="flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-3xl border border-cynBorderHover/40 bg-cynBgItem p-4"
>
  ...
</div>
<p
  class="text-xs lg:text-base font-light text-cynTextPrimary leading-5 lg:leading-7"
>
  ...
</p>
```

```php
<a href="..." class="primary-button btn-have-icon !py-2 !px-3 lg:!px-5">...</a>
```

## Use style.css only when inline is not enough

- Reusable component classes used in many places (e.g. `.primary-button`, `.blog-archive-tab`)
- Pseudo-elements (`::before`, `::after`) and complex sibling selectors
- Animations/transitions that need keyframes or multi-property `transition` blocks
- Third-party library overrides (Swiper, etc.)
- State combinations too verbose or impossible as utilities alone

## Don't

```css
/* ❌ One-off layout/spacing/color that belongs on the element */
.my-section-title {
  @apply text-2xl font-bold text-cynTextPrimary;
}
```

```html
<!-- ❌ Extra class just to move inline utilities into CSS -->
<div class="structure-review-card">...</div>
```

## Quick check

1. Can this be done with Tailwind classes on the tag? → use inline classes
2. Is it shared, pseudo-element, or animation-heavy? → `style.css` is OK
